Station Egwi, Etche LGA, exhibits a monotonic increase in resistivity through all interpreted layers. The resistivity values start at 295.88 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (Layer 1) and increase through Layer 2 (798.6 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$), Layer 3 (864.62 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$), Layer 4 (1810.2 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$), and Layer 5 (5634.2 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$). 

Based on the vertical electrical sounding (VES) curve-type notation, each consecutive triplet of layers follows the $r_1 < r_2 < r_3$ pattern (specifically, the sequences 1-2-3, 2-3-4, and 3-4-5 are all increasing), which yields an "AAA" sequence. According to the notation rules, this simplifies to a single "A" classification. This is consistent with the A-type classification currently recorded on file.

